WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.267
We're joined by CNN military

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.236
analyst, retired Air Force,

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.138
Air Force Colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.339
Good to have you with us.

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:06.806
Colonel,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.341
I want to get your thoughts, Colonel,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.276
on this long running feud

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.578
between promotion

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.580
and the defense minister show Shoigu.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:16.282
It's clear from this posturing,

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.250
if we can call it that

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.551
the president thinks

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.821
he can run this war better Given Russia's

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.356
reliance on Wagner,

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:23.990
who do you think

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:25.458
is coming out on top here?

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:27.627
And where does this end for promotion?

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.562
What is his aim

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:31.331
Yeah, that's

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:32.866
a very good question, Christine.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.134
It's great to be with you.

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:37.170
The basic problem that the Russians have,

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.205
of course, is that their normal military,

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:40.740
the regular armed forces,

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.441
those that belong

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.776
to the Ministry of Defense,

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:43.710
have not performed

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.079
well at all in the aggregate.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.280
When you look at the totality

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.314
of the war in Ukraine.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:51.384
So what precautions aim appears to be

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:55.355
is that he wants to not only tout himself

00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:56.256
as being,

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.557
in essence, a warlord

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.526
or a commander of troops

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.561
someone who can actually get things done

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.363
in the Ukrainian theater,

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:04.397
but also somebody

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:06.032
who is positioning himself

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.134
to replace, at a minimum,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.969
the ministry of defense

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:13.807
as the actual force and possibly subsume

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.575
the powers of the Ministry of Defense

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.576
and the general staff

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.710
of the Russian army,

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.412
and then potentially

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.980
put himself in line

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.116
for succession to Putin.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:26.252
So this is one of those situations where

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.488
you have a very ambitious person

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.057
who has to tread very carefully

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:34.561
and in very a clearly dangerous

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.396
world of intrigue

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.865
within the Russian political hierarchy.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.366
But then at the other end

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:41.401
of the spectrum,

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.470
he also has to prove himself

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.071
to be a man of action

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:47.006
and a man who can get things done.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.208
And this is

00:01:48.208 --> 00:01:49.242
precisely the role

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.643
that he is seeking for himself,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:51.811
whether or not he succeeds.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:52.712
Of course, it's

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.080
a completely different question,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:54.948
but that seems to be

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.549
where promotion is going.

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:56.850
Yeah.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:58.751
Second in line to Putin is quite a name

00:01:58.751 --> 00:01:59.385
and one wonders

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.554
how Putin is viewing this

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.656
to the battle for back meat.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:05.458
Colonel, we heard President Lansky,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:06.059
of course,

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.161
recommitting to continue that fight

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.762
for a back boot.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.030
How probable is it

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.299
that Ukraine are publicly committing

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.267
to continue the fight

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.568
while privately accepting

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:16.903
that they're going to have to withdraw

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:17.737
quite soon

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:19.172
and in fact, are even making

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.306
plans for that right now?

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:22.742
Yeah.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.010
So that always

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.045
presents a problem

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.347
when the public is watching

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.581
something like this.

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.017
They hear the public pronouncements and,

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.185
you know, the idea that,

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:34.220
you know, we're going to make our stand.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.789
You know,
the slogan in Ukraine being

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.725
Bermuda still stands.

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:42.262
That is a bit of a dangerous situation

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:44.063
politically and

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.432
from a moral standpoint as well.

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.067
So the best way, I think,

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.069
for the Ukrainian leadership

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:50.770
to move forward

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.172
in this particular case

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.507
is to accept military reality,

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.176
to move their troops,

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:58.278
save as many as they possibly can

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.347
and use their new defensive positions

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.550
which I would say would be best

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.084
to the west of parliament.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:08.221
I use those as a springboard to capture

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.456
and possibly even encircle

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.092
some Russian forces as they move forward

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:15.361
and then use it as a springboard

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.463
for a further offensive

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.565
during the springtime.

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:21.234
So that's a bit of an ambitious goal,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.602
but it's something that the Ukrainians,

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:24.537
if they get

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:25.371
the right

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.773
supplies from the West,

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.408
if they are resupplied

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.577
with ammunition, with weapons systems,

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:33.613
such as drones, AI and possibly

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:34.781
other things,

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:35.582
but they're definitely going

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.584
to get drones and artillery shells.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.551
So these are going to be

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.752
the important things

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.554
that they will need in order to prosecute

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.823
at least part of the counteroffensive.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:44.657
And that's really what

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.459
they should be focused on.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.760
And on your point, Colonel,

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.962
on the counter-offensive to come,

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.363
we know that the

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.764
the losses suffered

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.433
by Russia have been immense

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:54.300
on the battlefield.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.202
NATO's saying that it has been five times

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:58.271
that of Ukrainian soldiers.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.872
So even if Ukraine are defeated,

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:00.940
in bad mood,

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.742
how much of a tactical advantage

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:04.877
will they have in those counter offenses

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:05.678
to come purely

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.113
because they have ground

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.715
the Russians down and managed

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.816
to hold that line

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:12.752
Yeah, I think it's

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.354
it is a major advantage.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.589
Now, the one thing that we have to

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:16.923
keep in

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.558
mind is a bit of a caveat

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:21.928
is that the Russian personnel

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.263
strength is much higher

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.964
than the Ukrainian

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:25.832
just in terms of

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:29.068
the population in pre-war Ukraine

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:30.803
had about a fourth

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:31.671
of the population

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.106
of the Russian Federation.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:34.407
And about a 10th

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.442
the size of its defense budget.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.678
So that's the paper difference.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.079
However, the real difference,

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:40.847
the one that you see on

00:04:40.847 --> 00:04:41.881
the battlefield,

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.783
is one in which the Ukrainians

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.084
have a decided advantage

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:47.120
because they have tremendous command

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.454
and control capabilities.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.756
They give initiative

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.491
to the lower ones,

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.493
which the Russians do not do.

00:04:53.493 --> 00:04:54.193
And it's a much

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.161
better organized

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:57.563
military structure on the Ukrainian side.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.666
So the Ukrainians can use

00:04:59.666 --> 00:05:01.467
what happened in Bermuda,

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:02.802
as they've actually publicly

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:04.137
said, as

00:05:04.137 --> 00:05:04.537
a way

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.805
to have ground down

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:07.774
a lot of the Russian forces.

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:09.542
But they have to be very careful

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:10.777
that they themselves

00:05:10.777 --> 00:05:12.111
don't get caught in

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.780
that vortex around Bermuda

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.715
and that they can, in essence, live

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.683
to fight another day.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.885
Colonel, it is always very

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:19.285
valuable

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:20.353
to have your perspective on this,

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:20.820
especially as

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.789
we are
trying to figure out what comes next.

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:23.823
Thank you for your time.

